// ============================================================================
// DAILY — 2026-11-05 (Thursday): Pure math sequence — the look-and-say
// sequence ("audioactive decay", OEIS A005150)
// ============================================================================
//
// THE SEQUENCE: a(1) = 1. Each later term describes the RUN-LENGTHS of the
// digits in the term before it: "1" has one run of one '1' -> "11". "11" has
// one run of two '1's -> "21". Verified by hand, term by term:
//   a(1)=1  a(2)=11  a(3)=21  a(4)=1211  a(5)=111221  a(6)=312211
//
// CONWAY'S COSMOLOGICAL THEOREM: for this sequence, no digit greater than 3
// ever appears, however far you iterate it. Terms 1-5 above only ever contain
// 1s and 2s — term 6 is the first time a '3' shows up at all (its very first
// digit). That fact drives this piece's ending (see CODA below).
//
// PITCH + RHYTHM, both read straight off the digits — no transform:
// each RUN in a term becomes one melodic cell. The run's DIGIT (1, 2, or 3)
// picks the scale degree, skipping by thirds (0, 2, 4) so the sequence's own
// 3-digit alphabet literally traces out a triad. The run's COUNT becomes how
// many times that pitch actually repeats (`!count`) — "two 1s" is heard as
// two quick notes, not one note held twice as long. A "~" closes every
// generation, pacing the piece like reading the terms aloud with a breath
// between each one.
//
// Generation-by-generation (runs used to build the NEXT term):
//   step1 (1->11):      run(1,'1')                  -> one note
//   step2 (11->21):     run(2,'1')                  -> doubled note
//   step3 (21->1211):   run(1,'2') run(1,'1')        -> leap up, resolve
//   step4 (1211->111221): run(1,'1') run(1,'2') run(2,'1') -> restate+vary
//   step5 (111221->312211): run(3,'1') run(2,'2') run(1,'1') -> climax
//   CODA: term 6 opens on its brand-new '3' (scale degree 4, the 5th) —
//   the piece ends there, unresolved, because the real sequence doesn't
//   resolve either: it just keeps growing.
//
// JAZZ-IMPROV DEVICES: step3 is call (leap to the tension tone, degree 2)
// and response (resolve to the tonic). Step4 is motif-and-variation on
// step3's own material, extended by the doubled tonic. Step5 intensifies
// both ideas (triple tonic, double tension tone) into the climax, then the
// coda is a deliberately unresolved arrival — anchoring every step on the
// tonic (degree 0) as the anchor tone, with degree 2 as the recurring
// tension, the way a vadi/samvadi pair anchors a raga phrase.
//
// ARRANGEMENT: ONE voice only, square wave (sharp/abrasive timbre,
// MUSIC-KNOWLEDGE.md §1 — "power, action, intensity", fitting a sequence
// literally called "audioactive decay"). No separate drone: the voice's own
// delay feedback IS the growth metaphor — each term is generated FROM the
// previous one, so delayfeedback climbs generation by generation (the sound
// quite literally feeding on its own past), the same way each look-and-say
// term is generated from reading the one before it. NO DRUM LAYER: this
// topic has no metric pulse to track (it's a growth process, not a beat) —
// the "count" each run carries already gets its own audible outlet as a
// repeated note in the melody itself, so a kick/hat grid would just be
// redundant filler (see MUSIC-QC-LOOP.md's percussion-as-default warning).
//
// TEMPO: setcpm(20), 4 beats/cycle = 80 BPM (contemplative, not a dance
// tempo — this piece has no pulse to serve). CYCLES: 6.
// 6 x 60 / 20 = 18s.
// ============================================================================

setcpm(20)

$lead: n("<[0 ~] [[0!2] ~] [2 0 ~] [0 2 [0!2] ~] [[0!3] [2!2] 0 ~] [~ 4]>")
  .scale("A:phrygian")
  .sound("square")
  .attack(.005).decay(.08).sustain(.1).release(.12)
  .lpf("<700 800 950 1150 1500 1000>")
  .lpq(4)
  .delaytime(.18)
  .delayfeedback("<0.08 0.12 0.18 0.26 0.38 0.22>")
  .delay(.35)
  .room(.4)
  .gain(.5)
